# No default blue links

Default browser or Bootstrap blue link colors must not appear anywhere in GrayMoon unless a link is explicitly designed to be blue (for example the `--accent-blue` link style in grid cells).

- Every new badge, chip, button-like anchor or icon link that uses `<a>` must set its own `color` (white on colored badges) and `text-decoration: none`, and the rule must win over `.table tbody td a` in `app.css` (use `a:not(.badge)` there, or a more specific selector with `!important`).
- Check a new link visually in Workspace Repositories and Repositories grid rows before finishing: badge text must not be blue.
- Do not rely on inherited or default `a` colors.
